        "text": "The CWD model for the intelligent travel agent\nAs an example, let\u2019s discuss how the CWD model may be implemented for the intelligent travel agent\nsystem. The overall structure and flow may be as follows:\n\u2022 Coordinator agent : This agent will act as the travel planning coordinator. This agent will be\nresponsible for the following:\nI Managing the overall travel planning process based on a user request\nI Facilitating progress monitoring and effective collaboration among worker agents\nI Assigning tasks and coordinating the workflow based on the customer\u2019s travel requirements\n\u2022 Worker agents : There can be a number of different agents, each specializing in its own domain\nand expertise within travel and hospitality management:\nI Flight booking worker : Specialized in searching for and booking flight options based on\ntravel dates, destinations, and preferences\nI Hotel booking worker : Focused on finding and reserving suitable accommodations based\non location, amenities, and customer preferences\nI Activity planning worker : Responsible for researching and planning activities, tours, and\nexperiences at the travel destination, tailored to the customer\u2019s interests\nI Transportation worker : Specialized in arranging ground transportation, such as rental cars,\nairport transfers, or local transportation options\n\u2022 Delegator agent : This agent will act as the travel task delegator agent. This agent performs\nthe following:\nI Acts as an interface between the travel planning coordinator and the specialized worker agents\nI Receives travel planning tasks from the coordinator\nI Assesses the capabilities and availability of worker agents\nI Assigns appropriate tasks to the suitable worker agents based on their expertise and workload\nI Coordinates and balances the workload among the worker agents\nExploring the Coordinator, Worker, and Delegator Approach\n142\nFigure 6.2 depicts an extension and adaptation of our previous high-level CWD model diagram\nto this travel planning scenario:\nFigure 6.2 \u2013 The CWD model for the travel planner\nLet\u2019s walk through an example of the user requirement and workflow:\n1.\nA user approaches the intelligent travel agent system with their travel requirements, such\nas destination, travel dates, budget, and preferences (for example, family-friendly, cultural\nexperiences, and beach vacation).\n2.\nThe travel planning coordinator analyzes the customer\u2019s requirements and breaks down the",
